sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Shells as different in appearance as Cerithium, Solarium, Natica and Planorbis differ very little in their spiral angle (the ratio of radial to tangential growth) and differ in form mainly in the apical angle of the enveloping cone, which is set by the rate of translation along the axis relative to growth.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dissimilar turbinate shells share similar spiral angles and differ mainly in apical angle";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XI, “The Logarithmic Spiral”; topic “Apical angle of turbinate shells”. Scope: turbinate and discoid gastropod shells"
}
